# Design folder is the visual spec

Before creating or changing any user-visible component in `packages/ui`, read the
relevant files under `design/` and match layout, spacing, typography, color, and
interaction to that reference. Do not guess pixels or chrome from memory or from
other apps in the repo alone.

## Where to look

| Path | Use when |
|------|----------|
| `design/Tudu.dc.html`, `design/Tudu Android.dc.html` | Full-screen layout, pane structure, platform-specific chrome |
| `design/assets/theme.css`, `design/assets/tokens.json` | Colors, type scale, spacing, shadows, Dusk dark tokens |
| `design/assets/README.md` | Logo usage, theme import notes, radius and mono-palette rules |
| `design/_ds/modernist-*/` | Modernist system: variables, component markup patterns, interaction states |
| `design/uploads/` | Screenshots, pasted mocks, and palette experiments tied to a change |

## Workflow

1. Identify the screen or control you are touching and open the closest mock or
   HTML reference in `design/` (or a screenshot in `design/uploads/`).
2. Align implementation with existing app tokens (`@/lib/brand`, theme CSS in
   `packages/ui`) and with `design/assets/theme.css` / `tokens.json` when tokens
   differ or the feature is new.
3. Reuse assets from `design/assets/` (marks, lockup, icons) instead of
   redrawing or substituting placeholders.
4. If the repo UI and `design/` disagree, treat `design/` as authoritative for
   visual design unless the user explicitly says to keep the current UI.

## Constraints carried from design

- Zero border radius (no `rounded-*`).
- Archivo typography; mono accent palette; destructive reads via copy or icon,
  not a separate hue.
- Lucide icons; 2px rules and flush-left labels where the mock shows them.

When no `design/` reference exists for a new surface, say so in the PR or
review notes and mirror the nearest existing screen in `design/` plus
`design/assets/theme.css` until a mock is added.
